{
  "A4": {
    "answer": "The screening study in arXiv:2605.11724 describes an electride descriptor that begins with a Bader analysis of the electron localization function (ELF) to locate interstitial ELF maxima and then evaluates a \"figure of merit\" Z\u2091 based on the ELF basin charge. Although ELF\u2011based quantities are not present in the precomputed catalog, the same workflow first generates a set of candidate interstitial sites (void\u2011center candidates) before any output limit is applied. The number of such candidates therefore reflects the richness of the interstitial electron network that the ELF analysis would later quantify. This provides a strong physical justification for using the feature `cavity_geometry.candidate_count_before_output_limit` as a proxy for the ELF\u2011based electride figure of merit.\n\nGuided by the evaluation of my previous model (which showed little contribution from `pauling_electronegativity__min` and `neutral_assignment_exists` and redundancy between `max_clearance_A` and the mean clearance) and by the literature evidence that (i) a highly electropositive chemical environment, (ii) abundant spacious voids, and (iii) oxidation\u2011state imbalance are the key ingredients of electrides, I propose the following eight\u2011feature set:\n1. `structure_summary.pauling_electronegativity__mean` \u2013 captures overall electropositivity; lower averages favour electron donation.\n2. `structure_summary.alkali_alkaline_site_fraction` \u2013 directly measures the proportion of strongly electropositive alkali/alkaline\u2011earth cations that stabilize anionic electrons.\n3. `structure_summary.metal_site_fraction` \u2013 overall metallic character that supports delocalized electrons.\n4. `structure_summary.volume_per_atom_A3` \u2013 larger per\u2011atom volume indicates more free space for interstitial electrons.\n5. `cavity_geometry.sampled_grid_clearance_statistics_A__mean` \u2013 average void clearance, reflecting overall lattice openness.\n6. `cavity_geometry.sampled_grid_clearance_statistics_A__max` \u2013 maximum clearance, ensuring the presence of at least one sufficiently large cavity.\n7. `electron_count_hypotheses.total_assignment_count` \u2013 fewer plausible oxidation\u2011state assignments often signal charge imbalance that forces excess electrons into voids.\n8. `cavity_geometry.candidate_count_before_output_limit` \u2013 number of void\u2011center candidates before truncation; a higher count proxies the ELF\u2011maxima count used in the literature figure of merit and captures void\u2011network richness (0D/1D/2D connectivity).\n\nThese descriptors collectively cover the three physical pillars identified in the literature while avoiding redundancy. The added `candidate_count_before_output_limit` is directly motivated by the ELF\u2011based screening protocol, providing a surrogate for the unavailable ELF metrics.",
