      "reasoning": "I removed `pauling_electronegativity__min` and `neutral_assignment_exists` because the previous evaluation showed they contributed little to model performance. `max_clearance_A` was dropped in favor of the sampled\u2011grid mean and max clearances, which together capture typical and extreme cavity sizes without redundancy (the previous mean and max were highly correlated with `max_clearance_A`). The new feature `candidate_count_before_output_limit` is introduced based on the ELF\u2011based screening protocol described in arXiv:2605.11724, where the number of ELF maxima (interstitial sites) is a key component of the electride figure of merit. By including this count we approximate that physically meaningful descriptor using the available catalog. The remaining features preserve the strongest signals identified earlier (electropositivity, volume per atom, total assignment count, metal fraction) and together form a balanced, interpretable set.",
